" rx=\"46\" ry=\"19\" fill=\"#c8a26b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"-40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"9\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#f1e3c0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M-46 -6 L-52 4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M26 -12 L44 -44 L58 -40 L42 8 Z\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"62\" cy=\"-42\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"7\" transform=\"rotate(20 62 -42)\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"46\" cy=\"-53\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"3.5\" transform=\"rotate(-35 46 -53)\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"-46\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(260 140) scale(0.3 0.3)\"><rect x=\"-34\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"-24\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"33\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"46\" ry=\"19\" fill=\"#c8a26b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"-40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"9\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#f1e3c0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M-46 -6 L-52 4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M26 -12 L44 -44 L58 -40 L42 8 Z\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"62\" cy=\"-42\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"7\" transform=\"rotate(20 62 -42)\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"46\" cy=\"-53\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"3.5\" transform=\"rotate(-35 46 -53)\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"-46\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/></g><text x=\"70\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bed: timber</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">north slope</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Feed: meadow,</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">burn, cutblock</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Water,</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wallow</text><path d=\"M110 130 Q170 90 220 120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dusk: out</text><path d=\"M220 160 Q170 200 110 190\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Morning: back in</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Most elk within 183 m of cover (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Dusk: out to feed. Morning: back to timber <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Most elk stay within 183 m of cover <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Elk activity over 24 hours: two peaks, around dawn and dusk, from a collar study. Dawn: feeding in meadows and openings, then a drift into timber. Midday: bedded in cool timber. Dusk: back out to feed. In the rut, bulls move all night.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Elk day: two peaks</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"230\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"230\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">00</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">06</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text><text x=\"390\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">24</text><path d=\"M30 200 Q70 190 100 120 Q115 90 130 120 Q160 200 210 210 Q260 210 280 120 Q295 90 310 120 Q340 190 390 200\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\".25\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dawn feed</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dusk feed</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bedded in</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cool timber</text><path d=\"M30 170 L60 160 M330 160 L390 170\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Dashed: in the rut, bulls move all night</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the daily loop in detail</summary><ul><li>Elk feed in openings next to cover: meadows, burns, cutblocks, avalanche tracks (80%, BC habitat models).</li><li>Most elk occur within 183 m (200 yd) of cover (80%, BC habitat model citing Black 1979).</li><li>Where people disturb them, elk fed within 100 to 200 m of cover by day and went farther into the open at night (80%, Morgantini 1979, cited in a BC habitat model).</li><li>Summer: elk bed wherever they finish feeding, but close to cover <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Water: drink at springs, creeks and ponds; bulls wallow in the rut (70%, RMEF (Rocky Mountain Elk Foundation); Tip for drinking times).</li><li>Mineral licks: elk visit licks for minerals (85%, RMEF). A lick is a natural sit spot (Tip). Baiting rules: <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts\">unlawful acts</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 305\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A summer elk bed on a north facing slope under dense canopy, more than half closed, from a Black Hills study. A BC habitat model says elk use slopes of 15 to 30 percent most and use drops sharply past 40 to 50 percent.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"305\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Where a summer elk beds</text><path d=\"M20 260 L380 110 L380 260 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g transform=\"translate(80 240) scale(1.0)\"><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"-10\" width=\"6\" height=\"12\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M0 -50 L16 -10 L-16 -10 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(125 221) scale(1.0)\"><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"-10\" width=\"6\" height=\"12\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M0 -50 L16 -10 L-16 -10 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(170 202) scale(1.0)\"><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"-10\" width=\"6\" height=\"12\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M0 -50 L16 -10 L-16 -10 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(215 183) scale(1.0)\"><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"-10\" width=\"6\" height=\"12\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M0 -50 L16 -10 L-16 -10 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(260 164) scale(1.0)\"><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"-10\" width=\"6\" height=\"12\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M0 -50 L16 -10 L-16 -10 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(305 145) scale(1.0)\"><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"-10\" width=\"6\" height=\"12\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M0 -50 L16 -10 L-16 -10 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(350 126) scale(1.0)\"><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"-10\" width=\"6\" height=\"12\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><path d=\"M0 -50 L16 -10 L-16 -10 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(250 200) scale(0.35 0.35)\"><rect x=\"-34\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"-24\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"33\" y=\"6\" width=\"7\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3.5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"46\" ry=\"19\" fill=\"#c8a26b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"-40\" cy=\"-2\" rx=\"9\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#f1e3c0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M-46 -6 L-52 4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M26 -12 L44 -44 L58 -40 L42 8 Z\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><ellipse cx=\"62\" cy=\"-42\" rx=\"16\" ry=\"7\" transform=\"rotate(20 62 -42)\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"46\" cy=\"-53\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"3.5\" transform=\"rotate(-35 46 -53)\" fill=\"#5c3b1c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"-46\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/></g><text x=\"120\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">North facing slope</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dense canopy, over half</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">closed (75%)</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Slopes 15 to 30% used most;</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">use drops past 40 to 50% (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Summer beds: north slopes, dense shade <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Slopes of 15 to 30% used most <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-douglas-fir-stand.jpg\" alt=\"Dark timber: where elk spend the middle of the day.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Dark timber: where elk spend the middle of the day. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Matt Lavin from Bozeman, Montana, USA, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pseudotsuga_menziesii_subsp._glauca_(Interior_Douglas-fir),_Wild_Horse_Island,_Montana_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-subalpine-forest.jpg\" alt=\"Subalpine timber next to basins.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Subalpine timber next to basins. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Tim Gage at Flickr, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Picea_engelmannii_Pinus_contorta.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: beds in detail</summary><ul><li>Black Hills study: summer day beds were on north aspects, cooler than random spots, with over 54% canopy closure (75%, Millspaugh and others 1998).</li><li>Elk use slopes up to about 30 to 40%, most often 15 to 30%; use drops sharply past 40 to 50% (80%, BC habitat model).</li><li>Cover that hides 90% of a standing elk at 61 m is \"security cover\" <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Bedded herds have sentries awake (Tip). Walking into beds at midday usually sends the herd to the next drainage (Tip).</li><li>Better: glass the edges, wait for the evening move, or still hunt slowly on a perfect wind (Tip, chapter 9).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Evidence meter for what drives elk movement. Strong: dawn and dusk activity from GPS collars, and people and hunting pressure from field experiments. Good: deep snow from field studies. Moderate, mixed: heat pushing elk to shade and north slopes. Weak, no elk study found: cold fronts and barometer, and the moon. Short bars are Tips, not facts.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Evidence meter: what moves elk?</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dawn and dusk</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"48\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"48\" width=\"123.5\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">GPS collars</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">People, pressure</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"84\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"84\" width=\"123.5\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">Experiments</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Deep snow</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"120\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"120\" width=\"110.5\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">Field studies</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Heat: shade, north</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"156\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"156\" width=\"91.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">Mixed results</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cold front, barometer</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"192\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"192\" width=\"32.5\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">No elk study</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Moon</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"228\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"228\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">No elk study</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Short bar: treat as Tip, not fact</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Strong evidence: dawn and dusk, people, deep snow (80 to 95%).</li><li>Weak: barometer and moon (no elk study found).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: weather in detail</summary><ul><li><strong>Wind:</strong> wind does not stop elk, but swirling wind makes them hard to approach (75%, Colorado Parks and Wildlife). Steady wind is your friend (Tip).</li><li><strong>Rain:</strong> light rain dampens your noise and scent; elk often feed longer on grey days (Tip, hunter consensus, no study found).</li><li><strong>Snow:</strong> deep snow pushes elk down and changes what they eat (80%, chapter 5). In Wyoming, collared elk gathered in heavy snow (70%, Wyoming Game and Fish news).</li><li><strong>Heat:</strong> elk pick shade and north slopes on hot days and move more at night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><strong>Cold fronts and barometer:</strong> hunters often report more elk movement before a storm; no elk study tested it (Tip).</li><li><strong>Summer to winter:</strong> elk are most active in summer and least patterned in winter <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Evidence meter for what drives elk movement. Strong: dawn and dusk activity from GPS collars, and people and hunting pressure from field experiments. Good: deep snow from field studies. Moderate, mixed: heat pushing elk to shade and north slopes. Weak, no elk study found: cold fronts and barometer, and the moon. Short bars are Tips, not facts.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Evidence meter: what moves elk?</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Dawn and dusk</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"48\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"48\" width=\"123.5\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">GPS collars</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">People, pressure</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"84\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"84\" width=\"123.5\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">Experiments</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Deep snow</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"120\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"120\" width=\"110.5\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">Field studies</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Heat: shade, north</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"156\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"156\" width=\"91.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">Mixed results</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cold front, barometer</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"192\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"192\" width=\"32.5\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">No elk study</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">Moon</text><rect x=\"180\" y=\"228\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"228\" width=\"26.0\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"start\">No elk study</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Short bar: treat as Tip, not fact</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>No elk study links the moon to daytime activity (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li><li>Deer studies found no moon effect <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the evidence ladder</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Evidence</th><th>%</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Peaks after dawn and at dusk</td><td>GPS (Global Positioning System) collars, Alberta</td><td>80</td></tr><tr><td>People and vehicles move elk away</td><td>Field experiments, Oregon</td><td>85</td></tr><tr><td>Hunting pushes elk into refuges</td><td>Collared elk, Montana</td><td>80</td></tr><tr><td>Deep snow pushes elk down</td><td>Field studies via BC models</td><td>80</td></tr><tr><td>Heat pushes elk to shade</td><td>Habitat selection, mixed effects</td><td>75</td></tr><tr><td>Storms and fronts get elk moving</td><td>Hunter reports only</td><td>Tip</td></tr><tr><td>Full moon means less daytime movement</td><td>Hunter claim; deer studies found no moon effect</td><td>Tip</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Deer evidence: an Oklahoma GPS study found the moon phase had no effect on deer movements; weather effects were inconsistent (70%, search summary). Elk specific: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view. Before the opener, deer feed in an open field near the road. On opening day trucks park along the road. The deer move away from the road into thick timber. One hunter walks past the last truck, deep into the thick cover where the deer went.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#efe6cf\"/>\n  <path d=\"M240 0 L400 0 L400 300 L270 300 C 250 220, 300 120, 240 0 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".75\"/>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">thick timber</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"250\" width=\"400\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">road</text>\n  <g fill=\"#8b5a2b\">\n    <g><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"80 180;80 180;300 120;300 120\" keyTimes=\"0;0.35;0.7;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\" calcMode=\"linear\"/></g>\n    <g><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"130 200;130 200;330 170;330 170\" keyTimes=\"0;0.38;0.72;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n    <g><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"170 160;170 160;350 90;350 90\" keyTimes=\"0;0.4;0.75;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.4s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"40\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/><rect x=\"90\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/><rect x=\"140\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"254\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\"/></g>\n  <g opacity=\"1\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0\" begin=\"2.4s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Before opening day</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.4s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Opener: trucks arrive</text></g>\n  <path id=\"hf-pressure-shift-path\" d=\"M260 261 C 262 230, 262 200, 280 160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 5\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.5s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path>\n  <circle r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.5s\" dur=\".3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animateMotion begin=\"6.5s\" dur=\"2.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#hf-pressure-shift-path\"/></animateMotion></circle>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"8.5s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"12\" y=\"60\" width=\"210\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"117\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Walk past the last truck</text>\n    <text x=\"117\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunt the thick stuff (Tip)</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Pressure pushes animals into thick cover. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Pressure shifts elk to night and to refuges (80 to 90%).</li><li>After disturbance, elk moved more at sunrise and sunset <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pressure in detail</summary><ul><li>Hunted elk become wary, secretive and nocturnal (90%, BC account).</li><li>In the Starkey study, on days with ATV (all terrain vehicle), bike, horse or hiking activity, elk moved more around sunrise and sunset even when no people were out, as if pushed from their best spots <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Refuge use doubled during a Montana hunt <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>So: on pressured weekends, hunt far from roads and trails, or the edge of a refuge at first and last light (Tip). Respect private land; ask first (<a href=\"#/s/landowner-permission\">landowner permission</a>).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>When</th><th>Day pattern</th><th>%</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Early Sept</td><td>Rut starts; bugles at dawn and dusk; wallows midday</td><td>70 to 90</td></tr><tr><td>Mid Sept</td><td>Peak rut; bulls active all day, vocal at night</td><td>70</td></tr><tr><td>Early Oct</td><td>Second heat; quieter; feed and bed pattern returns</td><td>90 for heat, Tip for pattern</td></tr><tr><td>Late Oct</td><td>Pressure, snow; timber by day, open at night</td><td>80 to 90</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Rut bulls are most vocal at dawn, dusk and through the night (70%, quick lesson).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: notes</summary><ul><li>Bulls at wallows: may be any hour (70%, RMEF (Rocky Mountain Elk Foundation)).</li><li>Legal hunting hours: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset (99%, page 11, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">legal methods</a>).</li><li>The morning peak can come almost 2 hours after first light <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Do not leave your seat at sunrise (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Twenty four hour clock of an elk day in late September. Feeding peaks start after dawn, about 6:30 to 10, and again at dusk, about 17:30 to 20:30. Midday bedded in timber. At night feeding continues and rutting bulls move. An Alberta GPS collar study found peaks at dawn and dusk, with the morning peak almost 2 hours after first light. Times are a sketch, Tip.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">An elk day (late September)</text><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"165\" r=\"112\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">00</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"99\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">03</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">06</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"241\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">09</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">12</text><text x=\"59\" y=\"241\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">15</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">18</text><text x=\"59\" y=\"99\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">21</text><path d=\"M77.8 151.0 A54 54 0 0 1 183.5 172.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3d4a6b\" stroke-width=\"14\" stroke-linecap=\"butt\"/><path d=\"M203.4 174.7 A74 74 0 0 1 167.0 229.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"18\" stroke-linecap=\"butt\"/><path d=\"M56.6 174.7 A74 74 0 0 1 71.3 120.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"18\" stroke-linecap=\"butt\"/><path d=\"M149.2 236.5 A74 74 0 0 1 61.6 193.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"18\" stroke-linecap=\"butt\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"165\" r=\"36\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">24 h</text><rect x=\"258\" y=\"70\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"282\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Feed</text><text x=\"282\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">after dawn, dusk</text><rect x=\"258\" y=\"104\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"282\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Bed in timber</text><rect x=\"258\" y=\"138\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#3d4a6b\"/><text x=\"282\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Night</text><text x=\"282\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">feed, rut moves</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Alberta collars:</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dawn, dusk peaks (80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Out at dusk, in by nine, beds in timber, shade and pine.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 183: metres most elk stay from cover <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (tradition): \"Be on the glass before the light, and stay after the sun is up.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Strong to weak: light, people, snow; moon and pressure gauge, nobody knows.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 2 hours: the morning peak can lag first light by almost 2 hours <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 15 to 30: the slope percent elk use most <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion): \"Never walk through the beds at noon.\"</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion): \"The worse the weather, the better the elk hunting.\" Tip only, no study.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Leaving the seat at sunrise because nothing showed.</li><li>Bumping the bedding timber at midday.</li><li>Planning the hunt around the moon instead of the wind.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Next trip, log the time of every elk you see or hear. After a season you will have your own day clock.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>Ensing and others 2014, <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4160215/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GPS daily activity of red deer and elk</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>BC Species Habitat Models for Rocky Mountain Elk, <a href=\"https://a100.gov.bc.ca/pub/acat/documents/r1651/whr_4012_mceel_1098209135230_07a33d337dd7428586868202f6bc05bd.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">La Biche and Sandy Creek</a> and <a href=\"https://a100.gov.bc.ca/pub/acat/documents/r1583/whr_4069_mceel_1117055960977_ad101d33f76a47c38b67f114e5fbb078.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Muskwa</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Wisdom and others 2004, <a href=\"https://www.fs.usda.gov/pnw/pubs/journals/pnw_2004_wisdom001.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">effects of off road recreation</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Proffitt and Garrott 2009, <a href=\"https://arc.lib.montana.edu/ojs/index.php/IJS/article/view/2060\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Madison Valley</a>, abstract <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Millspaugh and others 1998, summer bed sites (abstract, search preview, 75%)</li></ul><ul><li>BC Ministry of Environment, Lands and Parks (2000), <a href=\"https://www.env.gov.bc.ca/wld/documents/elk.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Elk in British Columbia\"</a>, read directly <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></li></ul>","<ul><li>Rocky Mountain Elk Foundation, <a href=\"https://rmef.org/elk-facts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Elk facts</a> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span> and <a href=\"https://rmef.org/?p=15454\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">wallow report</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Wyoming Game and Fish, collared elk news (search preview, 70%); deer moon studies (search summary, 70%)</li></ul><ul><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, page 11, via <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">legal methods</a> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li></ul><ul><li><a href=\"#/sources\">Hunt Mentor research notes (summary of the sources listed in Sources)</a>.</li></ul>"]